ies": {"ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.8"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {}}, "order": 8}, {"mode": 0, "showAdvanced": true, "outputs": [{"name": "width", "links": [561], "label": "width", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "width"}, {"name": "height", "links": [562], "label": "height", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "height"}], "size": [677.2000122070312, 137.20001220703125], "pos": [-2895.102294921875, 5829.52099609375], "widgets_values": ["16:9 (Widescreen)", 0.6000000000000001, 32], "inputs": [{"shape": 7, "name": "preview", "label": "preview", "type": "RESOLUTION_PREVIEW", "localized_name": "preview"}, {"widget": {"name": "aspect_ratio"}, "name": "aspect_ratio", "label": "aspect_ratio", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "aspect_ratio"}, {"widget": {"name": "megapixels"}, "name": "megapixels", "label": "megapixels", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_name": "megapixels"}, {"widget": {"name": "multiple"}, "name": "multiple", "label": "multiple", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "multiple"}], "flags": {}, "id": 115, "type": "ResolutionSelector", "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.29.0", "ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.8"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {"aspect_ratio": true, "megapixels": true, "multiple": true}, "Node name for S&R": "ResolutionSelector"}, "order": 9}, {"outputs": [{"name": "text", "links": [560], "label": "text", "type": "*", "localized_name": "text"}, {"name": "show_help", "label": "show_help", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "show_help"}], "color": "#4b5563", "widgets_values": ["subject_definitions:\n\n[Video Reference] = the uploaded 10.75-second fight video. Use it as the strict reference for the entire environment, shot composition, camera movement, choreography, action timing, editing rhythm, body positioning, spatial relationships, lighting, dust, props, impacts, and overall audiovisual pacing.\n\n[Character A / Image 1] = the adult silver-white-haired woman from Image 1. Preserve her exact facial identity, refined realistic-anime facial proportions, red eyes, pale skin, long silver-white hair with symmetrical low side buns, pearl hair ornaments, long straight side strands, and elegant white-silver satin qipao. Preserve the qipao’s high collar, fitted silhouette, silver floral embroidery, subtle dark piping, long side slits, white high heels, and all visible accessories. Do not redesign or simplify her appearance.\n\n[Character B / Image 2] = the adult silver-white-haired woman from Image 2. Preserve her exact facial identity, soft realistic-anime facial proportions, pale skin, silver-white twin ponytails, black bows, white maid headdress, and complete black-and-white fantasy maid dress. Preserve the puff sleeves, white Peter Pan collar, blue bow and metallic chest ornament, white corset-like waist panel, small apron, layered short skirt, blue butterfly details, white knee-high socks, and silver Mary Jane shoes. Do not redesign or simplify her appearance.\n\n\nsummary:\n\nRecreate the uploaded reference video shot-for-shot and beat-for-beat, keeping the original abandoned concrete-building fight scene completely unchanged.\n\nReplace only the two original human fighters:\n- replace the fighter who begins on the LEFT side of the frame with [Character A / Image 1];\n- replace the fighter who begins on the RIGHT side of the frame with [Character B / Image 2].\n\nBoth women perform exactly the same combat choreography, movements, dodges, strikes, falls, recoveries, positions, and timing as the corresponding performers in the reference video.\n\nDo not alter the location, architecture, concrete walls, floor, windows, railings, boxes, debris, dust, lighting, camera path, focal length impression, handheld shake, cuts, framing, playback speed, or duration.\n\nThis is a strict character-replacement task, not a reinterpretation of the scene.\n\n\nretention_analysis:\n\nRETAIN FROM [Video Reference]:\n- exact 10.75-second duration and original temporal pacing;\n- exact fight choreography and interaction between both fighters;\n- exact starting positions and screen direction;\n- exact body trajectories, punches, blocks, evasions, spins, kicks, falls, and recovery motions;\n- exact camera placement, handheld movement, camera shake, reframing, tracking, push-ins and distance changes;\n- exact shot transitions and edit points;\n- exact abandoned unfinished concrete interior;\n- concrete walls, pillars, windows, upper-level railings and openings;\n- scattered construction debris and cardboard appliance boxes;\n- original natural overcast illumination and muted cool-gray color palette;\n- dust bursts and environmental particles caused by impacts;\n- original motion blur and impact intensity;\n- exact physical contact points between the two fighters;\n- original background and foreground object placement;\n- original audio timing, impacts, footsteps, fabric movement, environmental ambience and any existing music.\n\nREPLACE ONLY:\n- original left-side fighter → [Character A / Image 1];\n- original right-side fighter → [Character B / Image 2].\n\nIDENTITY / WARDROBE LOCK:\nCharacter A must remain visually identical to Image 1 in every shot.\nCharacter B must remain visually identical to Image 2 in every shot.\nNo face drift, no hairstyle changes, no costume changes, no color changes, no accessory disappearance, no swapping identities between shots.\n\nPHYSICAL ADAPTATION:\nAdapt the original choreography naturally to the two female characters while preserving the exact action path and timing.\nTheir garments and hair may react naturally to acceleration, impacts and gravity, but must never transform or become damaged.\nMaintain believable weight, momentum, balance and contact.\nDo not sexualize the combat or alter the choreography to emphasize the body.\n\n\ndetailed_description:\n\n[00:00-00:01.30]\nMatch the opening composition of [Video Reference].\nInside the same unfinished concrete building, [Character A / Image 1] occupies the original left fighter’s position while [Character B / Image 2] occupies the original right fighter’s position.\nBoth adopt the same guarded fighting stances and perform the same initial footwork as the source performers.\nPreserve the medium-wide handheld framing, cool daylight, raw concrete surfaces, debris, background openings and construction materials.\nCharacter A’s long qipao and silver hair move subtly with her stance.\nCharacter B’s layered maid skirt, twin ponytails and ribbons respond naturally to her movement.\nNo environmental changes.\n\n[00:01.30-00:03.20]\nReproduce the original exchange of attacks exactly.\nCharacter A follows the left performer’s attacking trajectory, body rotation, stepping pattern and arm strikes.\nCharacter B follows the right performer’s defensive reactions, blocks and evasive movement with identical timing.\nPreserve the reference camera shake and lateral reframing.\nMaintain the same distance between the fighters and the same position relative to the concrete wall.\nHair, skirts, sleeves and fabric show physically plausible secondary motion without changing the choreography.\n\n[00:03.20-00:04.40]\nFollow the reference movement into the section around the stacked appliance/cardboard boxes.\nOne fighter is driven or falls toward the boxes exactly as in the reference.\nKeep every box, floor object, dust response and camera angle identical.\nCharacter replacement only.\nThe collision must have the same force, timing and direction as the source footage.\nProduce the same brief burst of dust and debris response.\n\n[00:04.40-00:06.20]\nRecreate the close-range fighting sequence exactly.\nPreserve the tighter camera distance and vigorous handheld energy.\nCharacter A and Character B execute the original rapid strikes, blocks and body turns at the same speed.\nFaces remain recognizable even during motion.\nDo not change eye color, hairstyle, clothing structure or accessories.\nUse natural motion blur matching the reference footage rather than artificial slow motion.\n\n[00:06.20-00:08.20]\nMaintain the original medium framing and the same concrete architecture behind the fighters.\nReproduce the next exchange, including the original arm swings, evasive movement, stepping directions and impact reactions.\nPreserve the exact screen direction of both characters.\nCharacter A continues to inherit only the left fighter’s choreography.\nCharacter B continues to inherit only the right fighter’s choreography.\nNever swap their roles.\n\n[00:08.20-00:09.50]\nRecreate the dynamic leg attack / kick sequence from the source video with identical body trajectory, timing and camera tracking.\nThe attacking leg, opponent reaction, torso rotation, balance shift and follow-through must match the source choreography.\nCharacter garments react to the movement with believable inertia:\nCharacter A’s qipao hem and long hair trail naturally;\nCharacter B’s maid skirt, apron layers, ribbons and twin ponytails flutter naturally.\nKeep the action functional and physically coherent, not posed.\n\n[00:09.50-00:10.75]\nMatch the final knockdown and ending position exactly.\nThe corresponding character falls and rolls onto the concrete floor along the same trajectory as the source performer while the other character finishes the movement in the same position.\nPreserve the final cloud of dust, floor debris, background objects, camera shake, framing and stopping point.\nEnd on the same visual beat and duration as [Video Reference].\nNo extra ending pose, no additional shot and no fade added.\n\n\noverall_soundscape:\n\nPreserve the soundscape of [Video Reference] as closely as possible.\nKeep the original timing and intensity of footsteps, shoe contact on concrete, punches and body impacts, fabric swishes, falls, box impacts, debris movement, dust-related environmental texture and reverberation inside the unfinished concrete structure.\nMaintain the original stereo perspective and acoustic space.\nDo not add dialogue, vocalizations, magical effects, weapon sounds, or unrelated ambience.\n\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\n\nRetain the original video's non-diegetic music exactly if present, including its timing, rhythm, intensity and synchronization with the fight.\nDo not introduce new music, change genre, add vocals, or alter the musical structure."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "text"}, "name": "text", "label": "text", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "text"}], "flags": {}, "type": "CR Text", "title": "文本", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "rgba(21, 23, 27, 0.96)", "size": [688.0973510742188, 408.8326721191406], "pos": [-2891.531005859375, 6091.02587890625], "id": 144, "properties": {"cnr_id": "ComfyUI_Comfyroll_CustomNodes", "ver": "d78b780ae43fcf8c6b7c6505e6ffb4584281ceca", "ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.8"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {"text": true}, "Node name for S&R": "CR Text"}, "order": 10}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "image", "links": [675], "label": "image", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image"}], "size": [380, 90], "pos": [-4303.8671875, 4755.4501953125], "widgets_values": [], "inputs": [{"name": "da_model", "link": 673, "label": "da_model", "type": "DAMODEL", "localized_name": "da_model"}, {"name": "images", "link": 674, "label": "images", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "images"}], "flags": {}, "id": 349, "type": "DepthAnything_V2", "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "DepthAnything_V2"}, "order": 17}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "Filenames", "label": "Filenames", "type": "VHS_FILENAMES", "localized_name": "Filenames"}], "size": [400, 358], "pos": [-3823.863037109375, 4745.4501953125], "widgets_values": {"save_output": true, "filename_prefix": "depth/depth_anything_v2_24fps", "loop_count": 0, "pix_fmt": "yuv420p", "save_metadata": true, "crf": 12, "trim_to_audio": false, "videopreview": {"paused": false, "hi